    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (81.27) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headlining the lineup as the clear offensive anchors. Both players benefit from premier lineup positioning in the leadoff spot and favorable matchups against left-handed and right-handed arms with sub-optimal xERAs, respectively. **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42) remains a high-floor play against the soft matchup provided by Poulin, while **Caleb Durbin** (70.67) earns a spot start driven by a massive 19% boost from facing the struggling Sullivan. The emphasis today is squarely on mobility; with SB as our scarcest category, the speed profiles of **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Caleb Durbin** provide a structural floor that elevates them above higher raw-power alternatives.\n\nTactically, we are leaning into platoon advantages to navigate a tricky pitching schedule. **Dillon Dingler** (63.21) sees a significant 14% lift from the dynamic platoon advantage against the left-handed Rod\u00f3n, and **Nelson Velazquez** (61.05) maintains a starting role despite a neutral park factor due to his elite 0.421 xwOBA. Our most difficult decision resided at the fringes of the bench, where **Lars Nootbaar** (46.36) was the final cut. While his underlying metrics are solid, he was bypassed primarily due to a poor lineup placement in the 7-hole and a negative platoon adjustment, which pushed his efficiency below the established threshold compared to the primary utility options. Investors should monitor the status of **Casey Schmitt**, as his status remains \"Lineup Pending\"; while we are projecting him in the 3-hole, any deviation in the actual batting order could necessitate a re-evaluation of his 63.92 score if he slides down the order.",
